{
  "version": "kyberswap-v2",
  "namespace": "kyberswap",
  "description": "Per-namespace retrieval-verification dataset for the kyberswap namespace (4 live tools). Every live tool has blind rows (no brand word) and protocol-aware rows (brand named). Queries were written from the manifests and the navigation entry only, phrased the way a model would type them into tool search on the user's behalf. THE THREE CO-RETRIEVAL ROWS - \"swap tokens on Base, what would I get\", \"swap 100 USDC into ETH on Arbitrum, price it first\" and \"best price for a token swap on an EVM chain\" - appear VERBATIM in the sibling uniswap dataset, each expecting its OWN namespace's quote tool. That pairing is how co-retrieval is asserted: the validator refuses an expectation outside the declared namespace (`namespace-dataset.ts`), so a single row naming both venues is not expressible, and two rows over one query are. Together they say a blind swap query must return BOTH venues' quote tools in the top 5, which is what the 2026-09-07 equal-standing decision means for discovery.",
